---

<div class="space-y-16 sm:space-y-24">
  <!-- I. Preamble: The Tantric Matrix & Transmission Prerequisites -->
  <section
    id="three-kalacakras"
    class="relative rounded-2xl sm:rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10 bg-gradient-to-b from-maroon-light via-maroon to-maroon-dark border border-gold/40 text-white shadow-xl overflow-hidden scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-h)+4.5rem)]"
  >
    <div
      class="pointer-events-none absolute top-0 right-0 w-96 h-96 bg-gold/15 blur-[120px] rounded-full"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
    </div>

    <div class="relative z-10 space-y-6">
      <div
        class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-4 border-b border-maroon-border pb-5"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Dharmachakra class="w-7 h-7 text-gold shrink-0" />
          <div class="space-y-0.5">
            <span
              class="text-caption font-mono uppercase font-bold text-gold tracking-wider block"
            >
              Canonical Preface
            </span>
            <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-display font-bold text-white m-0">
              The Matrix of the Three Kālacakras
            </h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <span
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-maroon-dark border border-gold/50 text-xs font-mono text-gold font-semibold"
        >
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-gold"></span>
          Unbroken Jonang Lineage
        </span>
      </div>

      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-white/90 leading-relaxed font-serif m-0">
        In the Jonang tradition, the Kālacakra (*Wheel of Time*) is expounded as a threefold
        indivisible reality harmonizing the external cosmos, the inner subtle anatomy,
        and the transcendent path of liberation.
      </p>

      <!-- Threefold Matrix Grid -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 pt-2">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-maroon border border-maroon-border flex flex-col gap-2.5">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="text-caption font-mono font-bold text-gold uppercase"
              >1. Outer Kālacakra</span
            >
            <span lang="bo" class="text-sm sm:text-base font-tibetan text-gold font-bold pt-1 leading-[1.6]"
              >ཕྱི་དུས་ཀྱི་འཁོར་ལོ།</span
            >
          </div>
          <h4 class="font-display text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-white m-0">The Macrocosm</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-white/90 leading-relaxed m-0 font-serif">
            The external cosmos: planetary motions, astrological cycles, seasons, and the physical
            universe structured around Mount Meru.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-maroon border border-maroon-border flex flex-col gap-2.5">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="text-caption font-mono font-bold text-gold uppercase"
              >2. Inner Kālacakra</span
            >
            <span lang="bo" class="text-sm sm:text-base font-tibetan text-gold font-bold pt-1 leading-[1.6]"
              >ནང་དུས་ཀྱི་འཁོར་ལོ།</span
            >
          </div>
          <h4 class="font-display text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-white m-0">The Microcosm</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-white/90 leading-relaxed m-0 font-serif">
            The psycho-physical human body: the 72,000 subtle channels (<GlossaryTerm id="nadi" class="text-white hover:text-gold border-gold/60"><em>nāḍī</em></GlossaryTerm>), 21,600 daily
            breaths (<GlossaryTerm id="prana" class="text-white hover:text-gold border-gold/60"><em>prāṇa</em></GlossaryTerm>), and essential drops (<GlossaryTerm id="bindu" class="text-white hover:text-gold border-gold/60"><em>bindu</em></GlossaryTerm>).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-maroon border border-maroon-border flex flex-col gap-2.5">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="text-caption font-mono font-bold text-gold uppercase"
              >3. Other Kālacakra</span
            >
            <span lang="bo" class="text-sm sm:text-base font-tibetan text-gold font-bold pt-1 leading-[1.6]"
              >གཞན་དུས་ཀྱི་འཁོར་ལོ།</span
            >
          </div>
          <h4 class="font-display text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-white m-0">
            The Spiritual Path
          </h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-white/90 leading-relaxed m-0 font-serif">
            The contemplative method: the empowerments, generation stage deity mandalas, and the
            definitive Six-fold Vajrayoga <GlossaryTerm id="dzogrim" class="text-white hover:text-gold border-gold/60">completion stage</GlossaryTerm>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Lineage Transmission Solemn Requirement Callout -->
      <div
        class="p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-xl bg-maroon/90 border border-gold/40 text-sm text-white/90 flex flex-col gap-1.5"
      >
        <div class="font-bold text-gold flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>❖ Sacred Transmission Requirement</span>
        </div>
        <p class="m-0 leading-relaxed font-serif">
          This treatise provides a scholastic overview of the institutional curriculum practiced in
          traditional Jonang three-year retreats. Authentic practice requires receiving the supreme
          Kālacakra empowerment (<GlossaryTerm id="dbang" class="text-white hover:text-gold border-gold/60"><em>dbang</em></GlossaryTerm>), reading transmission (<GlossaryTerm id="lung" class="text-white hover:text-gold border-gold/60"><em>lung</em></GlossaryTerm>), and
          experiential guidance (<GlossaryTerm id="khrid" class="text-white hover:text-gold border-gold/60"><em>khrid</em></GlossaryTerm>) from a qualified <GlossaryTerm id="dorje-lopon" class="text-white hover:text-gold border-gold/60">Dorje Lopön</GlossaryTerm>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- II. Part I: The Foundational Accumulations (Thun mong sngon 'gro) -->
  <section
    id="foundational-accumulations"
    class="space-y-6 scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-h)+4.5rem)]"
  >
    <div
      class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline justify-between gap-3 border-b border-border/80 pb-4"
    >
      <div class="space-y-1.5">
        <div
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent"
        >
          <LotusFlower class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-accent shrink-0" />
          <span>Part I · Foundational Purification</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-display font-bold text-ink m-0">
          The Five Foundational Accumulations
        </h3>
        <span lang="bo" class="text-base sm:text-lg text-accent-secondary font-tibetan font-bold block pt-1 leading-[1.6]">
          ཐུན་མོང་གི་སྔོན་འགྲོ་རྣམ་པ་ལྔ།
        </span>
      </div>
      <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-surface-subtle border border-border text-xs font-mono text-accent font-bold uppercase tracking-wider shrink-0 self-start sm:self-auto">
        500,000 Total Accumulations
      </span>
    </div>

    <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-muted font-serif leading-relaxed m-0 max-w-3xl">
      Prior to admission into the Kālacakra retreat facility, candidates complete
      500,000 foundational accumulations to purify physical, verbal, and mental obscurations.
    </p>

    <!-- Classical Illuminated Manuscript Cards -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-4 lg:gap-4.5 items-stretch pt-2">
      {
        commonPreliminaries.map((p, idx) => (
          <div class="surface-card p-5 sm:p-5.5 rounded-2xl border border-border border-t-4 border-t-accent hover-lift flex flex-col justify-between h-full bg-surface shadow-xs">
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
              <!-- Top Metadata Header -->
              <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2 border-b border-border/80 pb-2.5">
                <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-accent/10 text-accent font-mono text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider shrink-0">
                  Practice 0{idx + 1}
                </span>
                <span class="text-[11px] font-mono font-bold text-gold shrink-0">
                  100,000 Target
                </span>
              </div>

              <!-- Titles & Tibetan Script -->
              <div class="space-y-1">
                <span lang="bo" class="text-base sm:text-lg text-accent-secondary font-tibetan font-bold block pt-1 leading-[1.6]">
                  {p.tibetan}
                </span>
                <h4 class="font-display text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-ink leading-snug m-0">
                  {p.name}
                </h4>
                <span class="text-xs font-mono text-muted block pt-0.5">
                  {p.wylie}
                </span>
              </div>

              <!-- Main Explanation Body -->
              <p class="text-sm text-ink/80 leading-relaxed font-serif m-0 pt-1">
                {p.purification}
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Domain Footer Pinned to Bottom -->
            <div class="pt-3 border-t border-border/80 mt-5">
              <span class="text-[11px] font-mono text-accent uppercase tracking-wider block font-bold mb-0.5">
                Target Domain
              </span>
              <span class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-ink font-sans font-semibold leading-snug block">
                {p.dimension}
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- III. Part II: The Hermitage of the Three Isolations & Dark Retreat -->
  <section id="three-isolations" class="space-y-6 scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-h)+4.5rem)]">
    <div
      class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline justify-between gap-3 border-b border-border/80 pb-4"
    >
      <div class="space-y-1.5">
        <div
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent"
        >
          <Dharmachakra class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-accent shrink-0" />
          <span>Part II · The Secret Hermitage</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-display font-bold text-ink m-0">
          Deity Generation & The Three Isolations
        </h3>
        <span lang="bo" class="text-base sm:text-lg text-accent-secondary font-tibetan font-bold block pt-1 leading-[1.6]">
          བསྐྱེད་རིམ་དང་དབེན་པ་གསུམ།
        </span>
      </div>
      <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-surface-subtle border border-border text-xs font-mono text-accent font-bold uppercase tracking-wider shrink-0 self-start sm:self-auto">
        50–100 Day Dark Retreat
      </span>
    </div>

    <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-muted font-serif leading-relaxed m-0 max-w-3xl">
      Following the foundational accumulations, practitioners undertake the extraordinary preliminaries
      comprising Generation Stage deity visualization (<GlossaryTerm id="kyerim"><em>bskyed rim</em></GlossaryTerm>) and sensory
      withdrawal within dark retreat cells (<GlossaryTerm id="mun-khang"><em>mun khang</em></GlossaryTerm>).
    </p>

    <!-- Two-Column Scholastic Exposition -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6 items-stretch">
      <!-- Left Column: Generation Stage Tracks -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-6 surface-card p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl border border-border shadow-xs space-y-5 bg-surface">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-border/80 pb-3">
          <div class="space-y-0.5">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-accent font-bold uppercase tracking-wider block"
              >Deity Yoga (Bskyed Rim)</span
            >
